<worksheet >
    <title>MD-2 Matrix Inverses</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete both problems. 
      Complete one problem with progress on the other to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
        <p>For each matrix below, use the indicated method to find the inverse, if it exists.  
          If the inverse does not exist, explain why.</p>   
      <exercise><p>Use Gaussian elimination to find the inverse <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="2">
            <mrow>A=\begin{bmatrix} -2 &amp; 1\\4 &amp; 3 \end{bmatrix}</mrow></md>.</p></exercise>
     </page>
     <page>
      <exercise><p>Use the adjugate (cofactor) method to find the inverse <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
            <mrow>B=\begin{bmatrix} 3 &amp; 1 &amp; -1 \\ 0 &amp; 2 &amp; 1 \\ 1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1\end{bmatrix}</mrow></md>.</p></exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>